sfx2: under LOK no infobar is shown, so none moves the view

After a load an asynchronous SFX event appends the "macros disabled"
infobar (MacroExecMode NEVER_EXECUTE) and shows the infobar container.
No kit client sees an infobar: the kit sends none. The hidden window
still takes room, the work window arranges its children and the view
window moves. Calc ends any mouse action when its view window moves
(ScTabViewShell::Move -> StopMarking), so when that idle ran between
a button-down and its up, a double-click on a shape never opened its
text, and a drag or a range selection stopped early. The ElyTable
test that double-clicks a shape and types failed on loaded machines
this way (Ely R19.8). The trace, by the fonts agent with gdb:
BrkDragObj <- DrawEndAction <- ScGridWindow::StopMarking <-
ScTabViewShell::Move <- OuterResizePixel <- SfxViewFrame::Resize <-
SetToolSpaceBorderPixel_Impl <- ArrangeChildren_Impl, between the
down and the up.

Under the kit AppendInfoBar adds no bar and UpdateInfoBar shows no
container. Every caller already takes a null bar; the UNO
XInfobarProvider::appendInfobar throws, as when the bar is off.
Under full-CPU load on 32 threads the test failed 8 of 360
runs without this and passed 360 of 360 with it.

